cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "CuHalide Atlas is currently a prepublication review resource, not a formally deposited public dataset. For living-atlas results shared during review, report the access date and Current Curated revision. Archived scientific snapshot 3.0.2 remains the immutable historical baseline for exact reproduction."
title: "CuHalide Atlas"
version: "Current Curated rev.10 (prepublication review)"
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "CuHalide Atlas Project"
url: "https://cuhalide-atlas-v3.vercel.app/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zion0321/CuHalide-Atlas"
abstract: >-
  Prepublication review resource for an evidence-grounded, structure-resolved
  knowledge base covering organic-containing Cu(I) chlorides, bromides and
  iodides. Current Curated rev.10 is reviewed through 2026-09-14 and preserves
  the immutable archived scientific snapshot 3.0.2 while incorporating
  primary-evidence-backed corrections, owner-approved corpus membership changes,
  and newly recovered crystallographic evidence. Reported composition, local
  Cu-X motif, global connectivity dimensionality, article-level retrieval
  classes, organic-component connectivity and photophysical measurements remain
  separated at their appropriate evidence grain. Structured Photophysics 1.4.0
  publishes data-bearing article states only after two-pass verification;
  Organic Components 1.2.0 remains fail-closed when molecular connectivity is
  not uniquely verified. Direct-link review access is query-and-view;
  search-engine indexing, bulk normalized exports, exact stored publisher
  abstracts, primary PDF/SI/CIF files and internal curation/audit artifacts
  remain outside the public release boundary. No permanent DOI, blanket license
  or formal public-release date is asserted until owner approval.
keywords:
  - copper(I) halide
  - Cu(I)-I
  - copper iodide
  - crystallography
  - luminescence
  - self-trapped exciton
  - scientific knowledge portal
  - retrieval-augmented generation
